-- Refs #182 (pool data inconsistencies, part: dead empty pools whose mother is also dead or absent)
-- ERROR CLASS: "Pool Id N is empty (has no creatures and no gameobects and either no child pools or child pools are all empty. The pool will not be spawned" (PoolMgr.cpp:743).
-- These 361 pool_template rows can never spawn anything: they have no pool_creature / pool_gameobject / pool_quest rows, and every child pool
--   (if any) is itself in this list. The same is true in the MoP 5.4.8 data (it has no members for any of them either, apart from 6 pool_creature rows
--   of pool 9868 whose creature guids do not exist in LoA), and none is in game_event_pool. They are leftovers from the TrinityCore pool tables whose
--   gameobject/creature spawns the MoP world DB does not carry. Multi-map splitting (_40.._43) does not change this: the empties had no members before.
-- BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL: none of these pools has a live sibling, so no other pool's spawn odds change.
-- ROWS: 361 pool_template + their pool_pool rows (as child or as mother).
